# Development Workflow Rules

## Development Process
- Follow a stateful development approach
- Define clear phases with acceptance criteria
- Structure project plans hierarchically as Phase → Task → Steps
- Each phase should have its own document with bidirectional links (parent/child)
- Each task should have explicit acceptance criteria 
- Each task should have a checkpoint for creating a commit after completion
- Each phase should end with a pull request for review
- Track progress against implementation plan
- Focus on implementation and the critical path
- When encountering critical things decide if they can be addressed later
- At the end of each phase check if we need to revise the plan before entering the next phase
- Use TDD for critical functionality - use tests as an automated acceptance criteria to know when the task is done
- Prefer end to end tests over unit tests
- Update documentation as part of implementation

## Version Control
- Use descriptive branch names
- Keep commits focused on single changes
- Write clear commit messages with context
- Use pull requests for code review
- Ensure tests pass before merging
- When pushing a commit on a branch that has an existing PR, also update the correct file in reports/ and the pr description to keep it in sync with the additional changes
- Follow detailed commit practices in [commit-practices.mdc](./commit-practices.mdc)

## Code Quality
- Run linters and formatters before committing
- Ensure all tests pass locally before pushing
- Address tech debt in accordance with the plan
- Follow the same standards for both human and AI-written code
- Review code for security issues

## Collaboration
- Document blocking issues promptly
- Update shared documentation when making decisions
- Communicate clearly about implementation status
- Seek feedback early for complex changes
- Share knowledge about patterns and solutions

## Continuous Improvement
- Regularly review and update guidelines
- Identify automation opportunities
- Document lessons learned
- Refactor code when patterns emerge
- Maintain knowledge sharing and documentation
